# Milestone: M3
# Covers: mytag.begin: / mytag.end: scoped hooks — body executes with begin and
#         end callbacks firing on entry and exit; tag.stop() interrupts end-tagged strand.
# blocked: v0.10.9-A (D4 deferred — 2 prereq primitives left: Tag.clone-fresh-sub-tag and t.name as a script slot; t.enter/t.leave are event properties now, top-level echo works, and % String format shipped)
# matrix-row: tag-begin-end
#
# Reason:
#   mytag.begin: and mytag.end: are method-chained tag scope variants that require
#   tag-slot access (mytag.begin, mytag.end as properties) — M4 object-model slot
#   dispatch.  Tag.new("mytag") named-tag construction is also M4 (Tag.new() method).
#   tag.stop() method call is M4.  The fixture produces complex ordered output
#   that depends on correct begin/end hook firing.
#
# Original urbiscript (activate at M4 with tag slot dispatch):
# # var mytag = Tag.new("mytag"); [00000001] Tag<mytag>
# # mytag.begin: mytag.end: {echo(42); 42};
# # [00000002] *** mytag: begin
# # [00000003] *** 42
# # [00000004] *** mytag: end
# # [00000005] 42
# # mytag.end: { sleep(1s); echo("OH NOZ!") }, mytag.stop();
# # [00000006] *** mytag: end
# # sleep(100ms);
